<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alberico I Cybo-Malaspina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1534">1534</a>–<a href="/years/1623">1623</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alberico I Cybo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaspina">Malaspina</a> was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massa-tuscany">Massa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrara">Carrara</a>, inheriting the Malaspina lands through his mother Ricciarda. He was made prince of Massa by the emperor in 1568 and ruled for nearly sixty years, rebuilding Massa with a new planned town centre and expanding the marble trade of Carrara.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alberico-i-cybo-malaspina.jpg" alt="Alberico I Cybo-Malaspina" width="300" height="554" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alberico_I_Cybo-Malaspina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
